# devanagari-manuscript-ocr (this folder: manuscript_ocr) — a generic Sanskrit manuscript OCR tool. Git keeps the code
# and its documentation only. Manuscript data of any kind (images, segmentations, readings, corrections, TEI, review
# verdicts, trained weights) lives elsewhere: the manuscript data in its own repository, released segmentations and
# weights in another. Extensions are matched in either case ([pP][nN][gG]), so that a scan named PAGE.JPG stays out
# on any system.

# ---- Manuscript images and anything cut or drawn from them: they are not for distribution
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[pP][dD][fF]
*.[jJ][pP]2
*.[jJ]2[kK]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[sS][vV][gG]
# ... except the synthetic page made by the tool itself (printed text, no manuscript)
!/tools/fixtures/*.png

# ---- Manuscript text and segmentation, wherever a run leaves it: TEI and PAGE XML, line ground truth, packages
*.[xX][mM][lL]
*.gt.txt
*.[zZ][iI][pP]
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z

# ---- Trained weights: large, and published on their own (CC BY-SA 4.0), not in the code's history
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.mlmodel
*.mlpackage/
/tools/browser_bench/models/

# ---- Keys and secrets: the contribution key lives in ~/.config/manuscribe, never here
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# ---- Python environments, caches, system and editor files
.venv/
.venv-*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- Run logs and their one-off launch scripts; reports on particular manuscripts
/logs/
*.log
/LAYOUTS.md

# ---- Copies of earlier code, kept while the project had no version control
/backups/

# ---- data/: the manuscripts' own files (layouts, segmentation, readings, corrections, TEI, review verdicts, page
#      splits, trained models, the pinned Kraken model, contributed lines) are kept in the manuscript-data repository,
#      not with the tool. Only the description of the folder's layout is tracked.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
